  "question": {
    "text": "At time <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, a material is composed of two radioactive atoms <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math> The decay constant of both kind of radioactive atoms is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi></math>. However, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;disintegrates to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;disintegrates to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math>. Which of the following figures represents the evolution of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mfenced><mn>0</mn></mfenced></mrow></mfrac></math> with respect to time <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math>?",
